{"id":"nabal","name":"Nabal","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:nabal"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Nabal","text":"Foolish, a descendant of Caleb who dwelt at Maon (1 Sam. 25), the modern Main, 7 miles south-east of Hebron. He was “very great, and he had 3,000 sheep and 1,000 goats...but the man was churlish and evil in his doings.” During his wanderings David came into that district, and hearing that Nabal was about to shear his sheep, he sent ten of his young men to ask “whatsoever cometh unto thy hand for thy servants.” Nabal insultingly resented the demand, saying, “Who is David, and who is the son of Jesse?” (1 Sam. 25:10, 11). One of the shepherds that stood by and saw the reception David’s messengers had met with, informed Abigail, Nabal’s wife, who at once realized the danger that threatened her household. She forthwith proceeded to the camp of David, bringing with her ample stores of provisions (25:18). She so courteously and persuasively pled her cause that David’s anger was appeased, and …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5037","lemma":"נָבָל","xlit":"Nâbâl","gloss":"Nabal, an Israelite","kjv":"Nabal","count":13,"share":0.35},{"strong":"H113","lemma":"אָדוֹן","xlit":"ʼâdôwn","gloss":"sovereign","kjv":"lord, master, owner","count":11,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H26","lemma":"אֲבִיגַיִל","xlit":"ʼĂbîygayil","gloss":"Abigail or Abigal, the name of two Israelitesses","kjv":"Abigal","count":6,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H5288","lemma":"נַעַר","xlit":"naʻar","gloss":"a boy , from the age of infancy to adolescence","kjv":"babe, boy, child, damsel","count":8,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H1494","lemma":"גַּזָז","xlit":"gazâz","gloss":"to cut off","kjv":"cut off, poll, shave, shear","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H5046","lemma":"נָגַד","xlit":"nâgad","gloss":"to front","kjv":"bewray, certainly, certify, declare","count":6,"share":0.16}],"verses":["1Sam.25.3","1Sam.25.4","1Sam.25.5","1Sam.25.9","1Sam.25.10","1Sam.25.14","1Sam.25.19","1S